The problem involves computing the factorial of a given number. In mathematics, the factorial of a non-negative integer n is the product of all positive integers less than or equal to n. It is denoted by n!.

A simple approach to designing the solution would involve using a loop that iteratively multiply each integer from 1 to the given number.

Below is a simple Java code snippet that computes the factorial of a number:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the number: ");
        int num = scanner.nextInt();

        long factorial = getFactorial(num);

        System.out.printf("Factorial of %d = %d", num, factorial);
    }

    private static long getFactorial(int num) {
        long factorial = 1;
        for(int i = 1; i <= num; i++) {
            factorial *= i;
        }
        return factorial;
    }
}
```
In this code, the `getFactorial` function computes the factorial of a number by iterating from 1 to the given number and multiplying the factorial variable.

