There are three methods to arrange the added three programs:
1. Arrange the three programs consecutively, which has $\binom{7}{1} \times 3!$ ways;
2. Arrange the three programs so that none of them are adjacent to each other, which has $P^3_7$ ways;
3. Exactly two of the programs are arranged consecutively, which has $\binom{3}{1} \times \binom{7}{1} \times \binom{6}{1} \times 2!$ ways.

According to the principle of counting by classification, the total number of arrangements is $\binom{7}{1} \times 3! + P^3_7 + \binom{3}{1} \times \binom{7}{1} \times \binom{6}{1} \times 2! = 504$ ways.

Therefore, the total number of arrangements is $\boxed{540}$ ways.

